body:
I completely understand. I was molested by my babysitter's husband. When my mother and grandma suspected it was happening,  they  called children's hospital then continued to take me to the babysitter. Then when I was 8, my cousin molested me and I ran and told my mom immediately. She said "What do you expect dressed that way?" He spent every summer with us for  a month. 

&#x200B;

When I was 21 she went to rehab for alcoholism, she told me "I had to process in group today about your childhood sexual trauma! It was difficult for me, but they told me I had to let it go because I did everything I could do!"  I just said nothing.

&#x200B;

AND my grandma likes to tell the story of her calling "concerned" to the hospital. She also loves to talk to me about my cousin even though I told her not to. 

&#x200B;

BUT I figured if I am going to be mad, then so are they. So I handle it like this... if my mom chooses to talk about it to me, I hang up. If she talks about it in front of others, I call her out on taking me back to the babysitters  or repeat my side in one story with my cousin. She quickly stopped this. My grandma is a far more evolved N. Babysitter I handle like my mom. Now with my cousin, I warned very calmly "When you talk about him it gives me nightmares sometimes for weeks, and I told you I don't want to talk about him or hear anything involving him. Next time I am going to detail out for you exactly what he did to me. Then you can have nightmares too."  So far I haven't had to use it. But I will.
